# This is a list of GPIO pins, set by the script /etc/init.d/gpio_pins.sh
# They are documented at: https://github.com/victronenergy/venus/wiki/bbb-gpio
# Format: <pin_number> <direction: in/out> <name>
#
# The <name> part is used to create a symlink in /dev/gpio.
#
# Pin choices avoid GPIO 16/17/18, which the spi1-3cs overlay (used for
# a dual-channel CAN HAT in Dual SPI mode - standard on GX devices)
# claims as dedicated chip-select lines. Digital input 4 and relay 1
# use the alternate assignments from kwindrem/RpiGpioSetup's
# gpio_listForCanHats for the same reason; relay 2 and the 5th digital
# input from that reference list were dropped rather than reassigned
# to keep this default minimal - edit this file directly for anything
# else. Same pin policy as raspberrypi4-64/raspberrypi5 - see those
# gpio_list files for the fuller rationale.
#
# NOT independently verified on real raspberrypi4 (32-bit) hardware -
# ported from the raspberrypi4-64 baseline on the assumption that this
# board's older 5.10 kernel uses the traditional base-0 gpiochip
# numbering (like raspberrypi2's existing gpio_list, unlike
# raspberrypi4-64/raspberrypi5's 6.12 kernel, which uses base 512 - see
# those gpio_list files). Confirm against /sys/class/gpio/gpiochip0
# before relying on this in the field.
#
# Digital inputs need a pull-up that isn't the chip default outside
# GPIO 1-8 - see the paired venus-gpio-pullups-overlay.dts overlay.

# relays are active HIGH
# Relay 1   GPIO 2 / header pin 3 (alternate assignment, avoids i2c0/i2c1)
2   out relay_1
# Relay 2   GPIO 27 / header pin 13
27  out relay_2

# Digital input 1   GPIO 5 / header pin 29
5   in digital_input_1
# Digital input 2   GPIO 6 / header pin 31
6   in digital_input_2
# Digital input 3   GPIO 13 / header pin 33
13  in digital_input_3
# Digital input 4   GPIO 3 / header pin 5 (alternate assignment)
3   in digital_input_4
